 ],
 "synopsis": "Gautam Adani-backed solar components maker Vishakha Renewables has filed its draft red herring prospectus with SEBI to raise funds through an initial public offering. The IPO includes a fresh issue of Rs 1,250 crore and an offer-for-sale of 1.81 crore equity shares by existing shareholders, including promoters. The company may consider raising up to Rs 250 crore through a pre-IPO placement, which would reduce the fresh issue size accordingly. Promoters and existing entities hold a 75.61% stake in the company. Proceeds from the fresh issue will be utilized to repay debt and for general corporate purposes, while proceeds from the offer-for-sale will accrue to the selling shareholders. SBI Capital Markets, ICICI Securities, and IIFL Capital Services are managing the IPO.",
